<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48929" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θοίν-η</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θοίνα</span></b>  (later <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θοῖνα</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			LXX
			<u>Wi.</u>
			12.6
		</span></i>, perh. to be read in <i><span class="en">
			Epich.
			148.1
		</span></i>), ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>meal, feast</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				114
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.119
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				9.82
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				350.7
			</span></i>, etc.: in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				530
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				B.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				18
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς θ. κὰτ τὰν ὥραν ἀπάγεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Michel</u>
					995
				</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>D</u>
				50
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θοίνῃς δὲ καὶ εἰλαπίνῃσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					239
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ θοίνας</span> after
			<i>dinner</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				148.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς θ. καλεῖν τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					1140
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ θοίνην ἰέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					247a
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρακαλεῖν ἐπὶ τὴν θ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				549
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκευαζομένης θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				178d
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1282a22
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τραπέζας ἱερὰς πρεπούσης θ. γεμίζων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					383.146
				</span></i>
			 (Commagene, <span class="entity">i B.C.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν
				θ. λέγειν τινά</span> to count as a guest, and generally to
			take into account, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				649a
			</span></i>: metaph., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Sph.</u>
				251b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				236e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				4.2.39
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>food</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτανοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					504
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Tim.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				150
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. παντοδαπή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Parth.
					12.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>feeding upon</i>, c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν σαρκῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Abst.</u>
					2.47
				</span></i>
			. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῶσθαι</span>.)</div>
